Moreover, entrepreneurship promotes competition, which is essential for driving progress and improvement in various industries. When businesses compete, they're forced to innovate and adapt to changing market conditions, which ultimately benefits consumers. This competition also pushes companies to be more efficient and cost-effective, leading to better products and services at lower prices.

